{"id": "EUVD-2026-103852", "enisaUuid": "815f8441-058a-3ffb-b3ce-6ed6087c6af0", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nusb: dwc3: gadget: fix IRQ storm on invalid event buffer count\n\nWhen dwc3_check_event_buf() reads a GEVNTCOUNT value exceeding the\nevent buffer length, commit 63ccd26cd1f6 (\"usb: dwc3: gadget: check\nthat event count does not exceed event buffer length\") returns IRQ_NONE\nwithout writing back GEVNTCOUNT. Since the DWC3 interrupt is\nlevel-triggered, the uncleared IRQ source keeps the line asserted,\ncausing a tight IRQ storm that accumulates 99,900 unhandled interrupts\nand triggers spurious.c:184 BUG -> kernel panic.\n\nThe resulting call stack:\n  __report_bad_irq+0xac/0xc8\n  note_interrupt+0x340/0x468\n  handle_irq_event+0xac/0xc0\n  handle_fasteoi_irq+0x120/0x228\n  gic_handle_irq+0x68/0x108\n  ...\n  kernel BUG at kernel/irq/spurious.c:184\n\nTo reproduce, write a bogus value exceeding the event buffer length\ndirectly to the GEVNTCOUNT register:\n\n  devmem <DWC3_BASE + 0xc40c> 4 0x1004\n\nWrite the bogus count back to GEVNTCOUNT to clear the IRQ source,\nconsistent with the stale event clearing pattern in\ndwc3_event_buffers_setup(), and schedule error recovery to\nreinitialize the controller.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:48:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:56:41", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/6cd82563bb270e03fe2f91324660ea14e3ce5d1a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/96918ca25ff467c25675478fc79393df4ae9d74c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ba927133b301894e7d24099afbb701887c8cd2f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f51cadb02b439850ab411df0a2cf4288a66d42e2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ff77cbefe5a653ea12874c213ea4bd0d72c1067"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98767", "GHSA-7v54-4578-623x"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0121940c-067c-3e3e-a432-2a70d65eadca", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.14.5 <6.15"}, {"id": "0c0a016e-e586-34b1-b30f-06271764e2c3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.15"}, {"id": "0c46b601-d64f-3cc7-8733-e5d1904929eb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "15b6d7b9-c627-3065-bb89-1d90fbb8cecb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.113"}, {"id": "194b04ad-ec01-3ad1-bde7-3d6a23f2c18e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2588a16a-ba73-3a4b-af81-29db22d4616d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "52a7c9d930b95aa8b1620edaba4818040c32631f <96918ca25ff467c25675478fc79393df4ae9d74c"}, {"id": "42a6ef2d-bef0-3f16-83c4-4f6fc3d6245c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a44547015287a19001384fe94dbff84c92ce4ee1"}, {"id": "71e07448-3a9c-37b7-b4f4-03da3a115a1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.136 <6.2"}, {"id": "7565e606-f59c-34ab-b9a1-d67bd3cda55b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.89 <6.6.160"}, {"id": "762beb2d-b262-3c9c-8f31-78eb60d00b16", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "63ccd26cd1f6600421795f6ca3e625076be06c9f <ba927133b301894e7d24099afbb701887c8cd2f1"}, {"id": "81263c5e-0c01-354c-a6bd-e194653bea8c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.237 <5.11"}, {"id": "8295ba99-cffa-30f9-ad4a-377cd5f54750", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.4.293 <5.5"}, {"id": "94bb1c0c-cbe5-30ef-8218-2a88be8d2cda", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.56"}, {"id": "a0452dae-0fab-3f53-9a61-ba0c1be422df", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name"